WEBVTT

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.960
What were you thinking?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.920
Do you think this lazy level
of proofreading is acceptable here?

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.510
Use your head!

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.750
I'm sorry.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.790
You're a professional, so act like one!

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.710
I told you this was due at 3 PM,
so why are you here now?

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.960
Everyone was waiting.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:17.790
Right...

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.500
If you're going to be late, then be late,
but you have to let me know ahead of time.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.090
There was a leak at my apartment,
my cell phone battery died,

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.160
and I got stuck in the worst of rush hour...

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:29.710
...is not what I should respond with.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.170
I'm very sorry.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.630
It's been a while since I've been reprimanded...

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.090
Yeah... me too.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.410
Is it just me, or are we the only ones
who ever get in trouble?

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:50.500
Yumi-san and Kaji-san never seem
to have anyone scold or yell at them.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.840
Kaji-san must have some kind
of diplomatic immunity...

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.880
Something wrong?

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.800
What are you two talking about?

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.130
Nothing really.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.080
Oh, she's already gone.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.670
Kaji-san is always so kind and beautiful.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:14.960
She always goes light on makeup
and wears conservative clothing.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.590
Despite that, she's like a fountain
of pheromones that spill out...

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.460
and attract all men making her
the most popular woman in the office.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.960
A man who can work, that's the type she likes

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.290
I psyched myself up and got down to business

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.830
But I'm always so busy and so bored

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.500
The company I work at now is pretty high level

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.710
And my dad has a lot of connections there

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.870
So there's no way I can quit

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:23.290
I'm always all by myself

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:28.460
I just take a bath and fall asleep

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:33.840
I can't even take the time to admire

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:40.300
Your hair or the way you walk

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.580
If all I can do is sleep

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:51.880
Then at least in my dreams

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.880
I want to see you

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.960
Incapable Hataraki Man

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.790
"Incapable Hataraki Man."

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.790
Did Kaji-san already leave for the day?

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.460
We just got a fax from Mogi-sensei
that contains his new manuscript.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.840
Maybe she doesn't need it...

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.330
Hiro Mogitaka.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.290
Known for his best seller "Snow in the Valley,"
which sold over 2 million copies.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.830
He's a super famous novelist.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:27.090
Currently, his serial "Journey of the Heart",
is being published in Weekly JIDAI.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.500
No! No, no, no, no.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.540
We need to call her and have her come back.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.830
I thought so!

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:37.800
Whenever a manuscript arrives, the editor in charge
should immediately let the writer know they got it.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.410
Afterwards, they promptly read it
and then contact the writer again.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.290
As a base rule, an editor must not
keep a writer waiting at any time.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:53.090
Kaji-san isn't picking up,
almost as if she doesn't feel the need to.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.880
Well, I suppose she still has time
before the deadline.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.710
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.300
She'll be fine.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.120
Not only do they not get upset,
but they're even covering for her!
She'll be fine.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:00.670
Not only do they not get upset,
but they're even covering for her!

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.300
Not only do they not get upset,
but they're even covering for her!
Hey, why don't I take it to her?

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:02.790
Huh? Why would you be the one to take it?

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.500
And they're excited about it, too!
Huh? Why would you be the one to take it?

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.130
Huh? Why would you be the one to take it?

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:05.590
I came up with the idea.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:06.620
All the men here are willing
to take on extra work for Kaji-san.
I came up with the idea.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.840
All the men here are willing
to take on extra work for Kaji-san.
I'll be the one to take it to her.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.160
All the men here are willing
to take on extra work for Kaji-san.
No, I will! I saw the fax first.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.340
All the men here are willing
to take on extra work for Kaji-san.
No, no, I'll call her and ask.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:10.910
No, I'll do it. It's better to be direct and not use the phone.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.710
They're content just to be able
to get close to her.
No, I'll do it. It's better to be direct and not use the phone.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.090
They're content just to be able
to get close to her.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:15.870
They're content just to be able
to get close to her.
Okay fine, but I get dibs next time.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:16.420
Okay fine, but I get dibs next time.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.050
They're enjoying this way too much!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.460
They're enjoying this way too much!
So, we're all agreed?

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.040
Doesn't it just make you angry?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.460
Doesn't it just make you angry?
No, I think I should go after all.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.840
Not really. I'm more curious
to know where she goes after work.
No, I think I should go after all.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.410
Not really. I'm more curious
to know where she goes after work.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.710
I'm sorry, but that makes you sound
just like one of those creepy stalker guys.
Then how about all three of us go together?

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:28.880
I'm sorry, but that makes you sound
just like one of those creepy stalker guys.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.080
It's not hard to figure out. I'm sure
she's going off to meet with some guy in private.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.960
This is Kaji-san we're talking about.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.920
I wonder if that rumor... is really true?

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:45.130
The one about Kaji-san
going out with Mogi-sensei, right?

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.920
That's just a rumor. It's not actually true, right?

00:04:49.210 --> 00:05:04.710
Kimio Narita (40)
Senior Editor of Weekly JIDAI

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.300
The women that I supervise?

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.170
I've never once treated them
any different than my other staff.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.750
Actually, that's a lie.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.500
It's hard not to be more considerate.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.670
Especially when assigning their workload,
or even just talking to them.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.250
Kaji has...

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:09.880
...really smoothly put herself into the position
of being able to avoid any actual work.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.250
Author of Weekly JIDAI's Serial
"The Eternal Daybreak"

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.000
Eiichiro Kitashima

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.170
If you had just called, I would have come
to pick you up at the station.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.630
Oh no, it's not far and the rain is very light.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.660
I heard Mogi-san is leaving
on a trip for Kathmandu tomorrow.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.130
Did he really send you two weeks
worth of material ahead of time?

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:48.750
This chapter was very interesting,
and much more intense than expected.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.540
These 12 pages are ready to go
without any changes.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.210
Thank you very much.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.750
As beautiful as always, that Kaji-san.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:13.630
Her very presence is overwhelmingly seductive

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.550
and yet all she ever does
is take my manuscripts with her!

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.170
I just can't stand it!

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:19.550
She already turned you down once, remember?

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.540
That was just some crap about how
she can't date authors who she does editing for.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.510
I tell you, that woman is no good!
She shouldn't be an editor!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.380
But Sensei, you never fail to meet
the deadlines she gives you.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.210
Because you always want to see her.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.710
Excuse me. I'm leaving for the day.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.630
Good work today.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.750
Huh? She isn't going out for drinks tonight.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.290
Senpai... she said the apartment above her had
a really bad leak that caused all sorts of problems.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.580
Oh wow, that sounds like a mess.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:02.380
Oh! So that's why she ran out of here
in a panic after that phone call.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:08.750
Apparently a water pipe ruptured
and leaked all over her apartment.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:10.420
Hey.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.960
You know that won't work as an excuse to be late.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.710
I know that!

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.050
Okay then.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.250
Why didn't you explain anything?

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:25.710
I mean, the fact that I couldn't
use my phone is my own fault.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.540
I also shouldn't have panicked
and ran home in the first place.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.840
These are all just personal problems.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.170
They don't have any relation to work.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:38.090
I don't think you have to be that strict about it.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.210
People will sympathize if you just tell them.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:44.710
I mean, you're a lady, so-

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:53.870
This is exactly why I said
I wanted to stay at your place!

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:55.420
I'm tired of dealing with it!

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.870
But if we just leave it like this today,
then things will just be worse later...

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.340
like the bed and the computer!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.210
Not to mention all my clothes!

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.500
What should I do?! I can't take this!

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.380
Calm down, Hiro!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.540
I just want it to all go away!

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:13.920
Putting all my emotions aside
and focusing extra effort into my work.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:18.920
I know that does more harm than good,
but it's the only way I know how to do things.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:24.090
I can't just put in a modest effort and still
be appreciated like Yumi-chan and Kaji-san...

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.160
I thought Shinji had come to understand that fact.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.800
This is the only way I can function.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.330
The only way...

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.090
Your hair... is soaking wet.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:51.250
It started raining harder than I expected.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.340
Hurry and take off your clothes.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.710
Gotansha Publishing

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:25.670
The cleanup took us all night to finish,
but now things are finally under control.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.880
Were you able to make up with your boyfriend?

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.630
Why are you assuming that we got into a fight?

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.290
Good morning.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.080
Ah, Kaji-san!

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:36.620
Hmm?

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.250
Yesterday after you left,
a fax from Mogi-sensei arrived.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.460
Right. It's okay, I had him do that
after he got ahold of me.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:46.500
Thanks.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.870
Whenever I'm near a person like Kaji-san...

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:53.500
I can't help but feel that the harder I try at this job,
the more harm it does to me in the end.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.540
Kaji-san.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.250
Hmm?

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.550
Nobody knew that you had already
spoken to Mogi-sensei about it.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.670
So everyone was a little panicked
when the fax arrived.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:06.300
The 3 R's... did they not teach you
those at the company orientation?

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.420
Y..Yumi-chan...

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.620
Where did all that come from?

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.000
Huh? What were those again?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.380
I think it was Report, Relay and... Review?

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:23.590
Relish. Rouse. Respect.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.790
Just kidding.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.090
I'm sorry.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.460
I didn't intend to cause problems.

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:37.920
Hey, Kaji!

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:41.550
This is bad! Mogi-sensei's plane...

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.090
they're saying it crashed!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.170
The plane Mogi-sensei was riding
on just crashed near the Himalayas!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.910
It was just reported on the Fuji Network home page!

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.710
Hey! Somebody open the
Fuji Network page and check!

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.210
Oh, I see it!

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:02.250
It's for real!

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:08.750
Plane Crashes Near the Himalayas
Novelist Hiro Mogitaka Reportedly
Aboard Flight 212 for Kathmandu

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.630
Kaji-san?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.500
Kaji-san...

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.710
How is she able to keep such a straight face?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:30.370
At times like these, I'm always calm
to the point where it annoys even me.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:34.130
But even if I were to cry or scream,
nothing would change.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:43.790
Meeting in Progress

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:42.580
On this trip, Mogi-sensei was going to be
accompanied by his secretary, Okada-san,

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.750
in place of an editor.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:49.460
I put in a call to his office in Tokyo,
but as I expected, nobody was there...

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.830
And the manuscript?

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.380
We only received 8 pages yesterday.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:12:03.620
He planned to complete the remaining 4 during his
flight and send them via fax sometime after landing.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.580
12 pages of a serial take up
4 pages in the magazine...

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.290
We have no other choice.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:18.010
Tomorrow is Saturday... Do you think
they'll tell us to come in to work?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.880
I don't think that'll happen.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.260
None of us are in charge of that project, anyway.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:29.500
Even if they decide not to publish the serial, there's
no way Kaji-san is going to write 4 pages herself.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:32.300
Whoever gets saddled with it
will struggle to finish in time.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.710
Shut up.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:37.630
If they drop the serial then they'll just remove those
pages, so there'll be no space for anyone to fill.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:40.170
And even if there was,
nobody is going to ask you to do it.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:43.460
Oh... I see.

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:57.130
Everyone only cares about the damn pages!
Why don't they worry about Mogi-sensei a little?!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.000
Mogi-sensei!

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.920
A BIG fan

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:16.170
Ultimately, Kaji-san is
responsible for the manuscript,

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.630
so why is nobody holding her accountable?

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:23.090
Normally, an editor wouldn't let their writer
go anywhere without getting the manuscript first.

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:26.910
But, Mogi-sensei told her that he would send
the remainder afterwards.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.420
She couldn't easily just say no.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:30.840
Are you the same, Matsukata-san?

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:34.670
The same as all those guys in our department
who treat her like some member of royalty?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.250
Well I...

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:44.880
I'm more disturbed by the fact that Kaji-san is acting
so casual despite that Mogi-sensei could be dead.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.300
She's a real mystery.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:54.460
Always the same calm demeanor.
Goes home without batting an eye.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:59.960
If I were her, there's no way I'd be able
to stay calm in that situation.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.290
How does Kaji-san always stay so composed?

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:08.000
I've never seen Kaji-san cry...
or even get angry... at all.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:14.420
Kaji-san is Mogi-sensei's lover... right?

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:19.510
If that were actually true,
there's no way she would act like that.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.460
Mogi's plane crashed in an accident... or so I heard.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.840
I can't believe that man would ever die!

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:49.040
And if I can't believe it,
then that means it's simply not real.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.630
I also have similar thoughts.

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:58.920
Then... that means he's alive
out there somewhere, right?

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.540
I was never really afraid of the possibility
that Mogi had actually died.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:10.370
After all, that man's existence
upon this earth is so deep and impactful

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.830
that nothing in reality could simply take him away.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.210
Toru Kanze (64) Painter
Member of the Japan Art Academy

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:24.750
In order to create anything, one first needs
a strong flame to help cast their inner shadow.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.580
Anyone who doesn't need
such a flame is a true genius.

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:31.630
The fuel to help burn that flame
can be mountains, villages...

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:35.090
rivers, animals... anything at all.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.800
Anything is fine, but women are by far the best.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.710
There's only one problem.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:47.300
Women sufficient enough to be fuel are rare,
so there's always competition for them.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.460
Oh yeah

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:21.290
I'm boarding the night train now

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:28.590
I'm leaving this town of memories

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.960
Matsukata, what's wrong?

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:34.250
I don't have any goal in mind

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.870
You look like a statue.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:37.670
Huh? No, nothing's wrong.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:41.710
I just entrusted myself to this swaying train

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:40.670
I wonder what happened...
It's rare to see her like that.

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:44.130
I bet she's still thinking about
the accident that happened yesterday.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:49.130
Words like "I don't know" or "I'm worried about tomorrow"

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:47.750
Senpai!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.330
If you've got puffy eyes from
a lack of sleep, use these!

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:53.210
Up until now, we've both hurt each other with them

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:53.040
Time for the meeting.

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:58.580
But if a night like this was looming,

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.880
We should've skipped those conversations

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.250
Why is it that despite everything that's happened...

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.830
I still insist on working?

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:09.300
We should have spent that time laughing together,

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:05.620
Huh?

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.120
Th-the meeting's starting.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.000
The two of us

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:13.460
Oh, right...

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:16.750
When this swaying train starts moving,

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.460
So... that's the situation.

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:19.630
I hear from beyond the window

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:23.840
For now, we'll have Kobayashi and Tanaka deal
with the four missing pages from the next issue.

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:22.800
Oh yeah, that cherished song

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:25.340
And also...

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.120
When the dawn breaks,

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:32.330
I hear from far away in the sky between the clouds

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:35.370
Oh yeah, a sweet voice

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:41.210
It must be you, baby

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:41.710
Your hair is sticking up...

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:48.080
Memories ride the night train

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:48.370
Kaji-san would never screw up
and end up feeling how I do right now.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:53.580
She would do everything flawlessly,
without having to make a sacrifice.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.960
I stay awake until morning

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.210
Why was I unable to handle it
the way that Kaji-san does?

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:05.340
Just gazing at the light of the stars

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:01.340
Are you okay?

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.250
You have an interview soon, right?

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.500
I'm fine!

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:09.540
Ah, it's almost time.
I have to get going to that interview.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.790
There was no particular reason

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:18.370
I just mindlessly wiped away my tears

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:18.500
What is up with that weird behavior and attitude?

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:21.630
Maybe she got the lead
on a big scoop somewhere?

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:25.620
Words like "I don't believe" or "It doesn't matter what you do"

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:30.790
Up until now, we've both hurt each other with them

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:39.590
Our job isn't to create anything.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.870
We don't leave anything meaningful
in this world, either.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.380
We waste a ton of paper every week.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.080
Just to pass on some useless information.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:55.580
So, at the very least...

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:59.330
I want to be able to serve under a real genius.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.370
I wonder if I'm just conceited?

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:04.790
That's it.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.000
It's finished.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:10.040
It's been a while since
I've painted a masterpiece like this!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.540
Somehow it makes me feel so clear and refreshed!

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.460
What do you think, Maiko?!

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.460
K..Kaji-san!

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:34.290
Apparently Mogi-sensei is alive!

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.040
He was supposed to be on that plane,

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:39.500
but his secretary came down with a fever
so they didn't make it!

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:42.160
Instead they ended up going
to a hospital in Bangkok.

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.870
Which is why they weren't able
to get ahold of us until now!

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:46.170
What a relief!

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.960
So these kinds of crazy coincidences
really do happen.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:53.250
Yeah, I remember how pale everyone
looked after that call yesterday.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.540
He really can't be more lucky than that!

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:59.380
Well, it still would have been nice
if he had called a little sooner.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.620
That's great news, Kaji-san.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:14.710
Matsukata.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:20.670
Just because you focused on your job,
doesn't mean it caused harm. Okay?

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:27.510
It'll definitely play a role
the next time you fall in love.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.660
I see... I get it.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.170
I finally understand what was bringing me down.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.580
Kaji-san is a real pro.

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:46.170
Not as an employee...

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.460
but as a woman.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.880
If Kaji-san were in my shoes,
she wouldn't have put him through that.

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.760
She wouldn't have driven him to say those words...

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.710
When I look at you, Hiro...

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:04.710
all I can do is be frustrated
with how incapable I am!

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.420
It's not your fault, Hiro.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.670
We should... just break up.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.370
Shangri-la

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:37.630
Even in my dreams you can't manage a proper smile

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:42.960
I just want to chide and love a hopeless person like you

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:49.960
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.500
Where shall we go?

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:59.000
Ahh... ahh...

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.210
Shangri-la

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:06.210
Let me hear you shout "I'm happy!"

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:10.500
Let me see the tears underneath your tough exterior

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:12.170
Shangri-la

00:22:12.170 --> 00:22:17.130
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:22.170
Please chide and love a hopeless person like me

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:25.420
Shinji
Nice Work Today
Do your best, but don't
wear yourself out.
-Shinji

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.830
Next Episode: Nevertheless Hataraki Man
